dium", "notes": ["Incumbent David Rouzer (R) is running."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's 7th District leans Republican by about seven points, and incumbent David Rouzer is seeking another term with a commanding financial edge. He has raised nearly $2 million and holds $2.3 million on hand, while Democratic challenger Kimberly Hardy has raised about $294,000 with just $65,000 available. A Libertarian candidate is on the ballot but has minimal funding.\n\nThe only public poll, conducted by Democratic-leaning Public Policy Polling in August, still showed Rouzer ahead 45 to 39. Rating organizations uniformly place the race in the Safe or Likely Republican column, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-seven chance. Headlines reflect routine incumbent activity such as grants and constituent services, with no sign of scandal. The main question is the margin rather than the outcome, though a strong Democratic national environment could tighten the race somewhat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0898, "margin": -8.11}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0938, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0915, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1198, "margin": -8.2}]}